		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=164&amp;p=736#p736"><![CDATA[
OK<br><br>I think there are some other bugs which can occur when operators don't setup the Contact for a Channel, or for the VFO channel (in the CPS)<br><br>In these cases the firmware will be using TG 9, but it should be using the first Contact in the Digital Contacts<br><br>I am modifying the firmware, so that if the Contact is not defined for a Channel.. When it is loaded from the codeplug memory, the Contact for the Channel will be set to Contact number 1, as the CPS guarantees there is always 1 digital contact as it can not be removed.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Sun Nov 24, 2019 9:18 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
